            </div>
            <div class="h-30"></div>
            <p>The challenge was threefold:</p>
            <ul>
                <li><strong>Operational Complexity:</strong> Designing <em>Pelican</em>, a native Android app for pickers, handling real-time flows: order reception, laser scanning, complex edge cases (weighable items, out-of-stock replacements), and massive inventory management (pallet receivings, Putaway processes, Cycle Counts).</li>
                <li><strong>Administrative Ecosystem:</strong> Creating a connected suite (Vendor, Store, Inventory & Shopper Management) so store managers could control P&L, stock, and staff.</li>
                <li><strong>Design Team Scalability:</strong> Amidst hyper-growth, the 20+ design team lacked a single source of truth and standardized processes to design with speed and consistency.</li>
            </ul>
            <div class="h-30"></div>
        </div>

